      "note": "RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe endpoint: the POST is sent server-to-server by the recipient's mailbox provider (Gmail, Yahoo), which has no session and cannot obtain a CSRF token - :exception would break the mandated protocol. There is nothing to forge: the controller is anonymous (no session state is read or written), and the action is authorized solely by the signed UnsubscribeToken in the path, which binds one (recipient, sender) pair. A cross-site attacker who has a valid token already has the unsubscribe capability by definition - CSRF adds nothing."
